{
  "action": "hold_drawer_key",
  "note": "The wire is safe and sound, but it isn't ours. The ident my brother cut is in that drawer behind the combination, and the vermilion tin is sealed up there with it. Eight seconds on the red lamp, Phil already on the live return reading the same grey copy every station reads. If I let the roster stand and walk away from the key, whatever is in that tin gets handled by someone who'll log it as 'misc. archive' and play it under a network tag. The archive is mine. I pocket the key, tell Phil the booth is closed for the rest of the shift, and I'll pull the ident myself when the clock hits zero. 'Your mic is still on, Mercury.' Let them hear it the way it was meant to be heard."
}
